A notification's description tells every bit, whatever the capability may signal once carved.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes
Witness: fuzz describe-every-type

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -940,7 +940,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) int cap_info(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t *a
         break;
     case CAP_NOTIFICATION:
         /* The bits it may signal, never those that are set, which only a wait takes, with RIGHT_R. */
-        arg[2] = cap->b;
+        arg[2] = NOTIFY_ALL_BITS;
         break;
     case CAP_IRQ_LINE:
         /* Carving narrows within one grant, so a range is all timer lines or none. */
